course: dictionary
lesson: 15962
title: Untrained: not yet taught
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of untrained is un-, which means not. Trained means taught or practised, so untrained means not taught or not practised in a skill, job or behaviour.
explain: «The puppy is untrained, so it jumps up and chews your shoes.» The clues jumps and chews show the puppy has not been taught how to behave. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "not taught" fits the sentence.
explain: «To the untrained eye, the painting looks like a few splashes of paint.» An expert would see the shapes and colours, but someone with an untrained eye cannot. Untrained can describe people, animals, eyes and ears.
fact: Untrained means not taught or practised.
fact: «An untrained puppy» has not learned to behave or obey.
fact: «To the untrained eye» means to someone who is not an expert.
fact: Untrained people should not do dangerous jobs, such as electrical work or diving rescues. They should call trained helpers.
exercise: «The untrained puppy chewed the sofa.» What does untrained mean here? | Trained to fetch and sit | *Not yet taught to behave | Covered in mud | Very tired
exercise: Which job should only be done by a trained helper? | Reading a story | *Electrical work | Tidying your bedroom | Drawing a picture
exercise: «To the untrained eye, the painting looks like splashes.» What does «to the untrained eye» mean? | *To someone who is not an expert | To someone wearing glasses | To someone who has won a prize | To someone who is very tired
test: What does «untrained» mean? | Very large | *Not taught or practised | Full of paint | Very quick
test: Jo says, «Call a trained helper for the wiring, not an untrained one.» Why? | Wiring is always fun for children | Untrained people are always faster | *Electrical work is dangerous for people who have not been trained | Trained helpers are cheaper
exam: «The untrained staff made mistakes, so the manager asked for trained helpers.» Why did the manager ask for trained helpers? | Because the staff had won a prize | Because the shop was closed | *Because the staff had not been taught the job | Because the staff were too happy
